 "content": "scripts/export.py produces the monthly invoice report that Finance imports into their accounting tool at the start of each month. It runs from the ops cron on the 2nd at 06:00 UTC and writes one file per environment to EXPORT_BUCKET under `exports/<YYYY-MM>/invoices.csv`. Finance reconciles the totals against the ledger, so every finalized invoice of the month must appear exactly once, including zero-amount ones; drafts are excluded. Columns, in order: invoice id, customer id, subtotal, tax, total, finalized date. Amounts are integer cents with no currency symbol. Format (Finance's new accounting tool, adopted late Sept/early Oct 2026): plain comma-separated (`,`), dates in ISO format `YYYY-MM-DD` (strftime `%Y-%m-%d`), UTF-8 without a BOM. The previous German-locale tool required semicolons and DD.MM.YYYY; that no longer applies.",
 "premise": "while Finance uses the accounting tool they switched to around 2026-09-27",
